# MASTER DEVELOPMENT PROMPT: BUILD A COMPLETE REAL-TIME FASHION COMMERCE & TECHNOLOGY ECOSYSTEM FOR BANGLADESH

Act as a senior product architect, UI/UX designer, full-stack software engineer, database architect, cybersecurity engineer, and DevOps engineer.

Your task is to plan, architect, design, and develop a complete, functional, production-oriented fashion-tech commerce platform for the Bangladesh market.

This must be a real, working, full-stack application with a customer-facing website, merchant management system, physical retail inventory integration, centralised order management, administrative dashboard, and integrated delivery management infrastructure.

Do not create merely a landing page, static prototype, or collection of disconnected dashboard mockups.

Every major feature must have functional frontend components, backend logic, database integration, proper permissions, validation, and meaningful user workflows.

Build the system modularly so it can be expanded without rebuilding the entire platform.

---

# 1. BUSINESS CONCEPT

The platform is a unified fashion commerce ecosystem connecting:

1. Customers who want to discover and purchase clothing.
2. Physical clothing retailers with existing POS systems.
3. Physical retailers without POS systems.
4. Online-only clothing brands and independent sellers.
5. The central marketplace and inventory management infrastructure.
6. Delivery operations and riders.
7. Platform administrators.

The objective is to connect fragmented fashion businesses across Bangladesh into one digital commerce ecosystem.

Customers should be able to discover products from different clothing brands, compare prices and product information, check availability, place orders, and receive products through an integrated delivery network.

Merchants should be able to participate without being forced to change their existing business operations.

The platform must support both marketplace commerce and merchant operational software.

Initial product category: Clothing and fashion.

Initial geographical market: Bangladesh.

Currency: Bangladeshi Taka (BDT / ৳).

Primary language: English, with architecture ready for Bangla localisation.

Timezone: Asia/Dhaka.

